WEBVTT

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.060
I really appreciate this.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.290
Even when you're not
in the mood to pilot Zegapain,

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.590
you still accepted this recon mission.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.300
There's something...

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.490
There's something
I just have to see for myself!

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:51.630
See for yourself?

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.570
The human race
was destroyed by the Gards-orm.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:58.170
All of us are living in a phantom
city that's inside a machine!

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.570
The memories of a dead human race!

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:04.240
You think you can hit me with news like
that and expect me to just accept it?!

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.380
You're right.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:09.680
Fine. You can look around
until you're satisfied.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.980
<i>This world must be the one that's made up.</i>

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.420
<i>That's right. It has to be.</i>

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.500
Vanish! All of this!

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.190
DISAPPEAR!

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.280
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.620
YOU GOD DAMNED FOOLS!

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:00.460
<i>You want Chris and Arque permanently</i>
<i>attached to the Oceanus's crew?!</i>

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.600
We're currently experiencing a severe pilot shortage.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:10.180
<i>Even so, the Dvaraka hasn't any manpower</i>
<i>to spare either, Commander Shima.</i>

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.670
Of course, that isn't the only reason for this.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:16.620
Both of our ships have
already moved further apart.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:19.720
Even if we tried an ultra-long
range teleport of the Hraesvelg,

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:24.720
it'd have so little Q.L. left that it couldn't
hold off any enemies it might encounter.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:28.520
<i>I already know the Gards-orm</i>
<i>are after the Oceanus.</i>

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.470
I'm sorry, Commander Isola.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.570
We'd like to stay here.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:36.700
It looks like we can destroy more
Gards-orm here aboard the Oceanus.

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:38.840
<i>You're both mercenaries.</i>

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:42.870
<i>You're free to choose which</i>
<i>vessel to serve aboard, but...</i>

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:46.180
<i>Are you really sure you want this, Arque?</i>

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:48.780
Yes. We came to this decision together.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:50.650
<i>I see.</i>

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:54.680
<i>Then sadly, I have no choice. Very well.</i>

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:57.660
<i>However!</i>

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.700
<i>Promise me we'll meet again.</i>
<i>That's my one condition.</i>

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:04.060
Thank you, Commander.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.840
<i>Still, even if it was a sneak</i>
<i>attack by Abyss and Sin,</i>

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:15.040
<i>it was a major failure to allow</i>
<i>them to steal the Zegapain's data.</i>

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.510
Yes. That was my mistake.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.810
At any rate, they're sure to
make some kind of move.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:22.890
<i>We'd both better stay on guard.</i>

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.680
<i>See you. Give Yehl my regards.</i>

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:36.070
Chris, Arque, let's make this official.
Welcome aboard the Oceanus.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:37.370
It's a pleasure to be here.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:38.060
A pleasure.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:45.910
In other words, these things are vehicles for
allowing ghosts to walk around outside, right?

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:53.450
No. The holonic loader is a life support system
to sustain your meta-bodies in the real world.

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:56.210
You could think of it as being
like deep-sea diving gear.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.220
Like we're alive...

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:03.260
Kyo, your facial color doesn't look at all well.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.560
Your mentalism level is also very erratic.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:08.120
Is your physical condition not well?

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:16.040
Believe it or not, I know quite
a bit about medical science.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:20.870
Let's see... Judging by your current
symptoms, my first guess would be...

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:25.210
YOU GOD DAMNED FOOLS!

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:30.780
Feel better now?

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.580
Did the Gards-orm really kill them all?!

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:36.760
Yes. They destroyed humanity.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:39.090
And soon they'll kill those like you,
who were evacuated onto the servers.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:44.000
But, that means I'm dead, too!
I only survive as data now!

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.900
That's correct.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:52.810
I've considered what may be giving
you trouble. There are 15 possibili...

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:56.350
Never mind, Fosetta.
I appreciate the concern, though.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:57.050
But...

00:05:57.050 --> 00:06:00.780
Besides, I don't have a body,
so I can't get sick anymore, can I?

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:05.620
Kyo...

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:10.260
Morning, Kyo.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.460
Oh. It's you, Kaminagi.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.960
What do you mean "Oh, it's you," huh?

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.570
Are you okay?

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:24.540
"Okay?"

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:27.770
Well... You've been really
down for the past few days.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:32.540
I have?!
Well, time to cheer up, then!

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:36.780
Hee-ya! Hi-ya! Oopsey-daisy!

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:38.980
'Kay?

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:42.260
<i>That's why I said you were acting weird.</i>

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:44.620
<i>You never do stuff like that...</i>

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:56.240
In short, this is a phenomenon caused
by changes in atmospheric pressure.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.940
Remember that, because it's going
to be on the exam. Okay, next...

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.870
<i>What the hell are we doing?</i>

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.520
<i>We're just ghosts, but we go on studying.</i>

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:10.180
<i>We have no bodies, but we exercise.</i>

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:14.220
It's all crap...

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:16.250
Ah, to be young again...

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:22.000
So, one week of staying after or a
mountain of homework. Which will it be?

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:24.800
Impossible!

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:26.170
IM-possible!

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:30.370
The sun could rise in the west and
that idiot would still come to the pool!

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.380
And for him to miss two days
of swimming in a row is...

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:34.810
- Totally impossible.
- Totally impossible.

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:38.180
Which means we've come
here two days in a row.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.280
This is lame! Let's go!

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.880
Huh? Hey, wait up!

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:51.320
This may be his chance.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:57.860
Sogoru's been acting weird?

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.670
He just seems to be kinda down.

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:04.230
As soon as school ends,
he just goes straight home.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:07.180
Sure he's not just having trouble with
Kawaguchi and the others again?

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:09.200
What was that about me?

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.570
Don't go telling stories about people!

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.770
Mind if we join you?

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:23.990
You finished? I'll take it, then!

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:26.850
Ushio, you jerk!

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:32.200
Um, Hayasechi, you're going
on to university, right?

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.370
Who knows.

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:35.910
No way! I hear you're a shoo-in
to make the final cut...

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.700
on the Tokyo University entrance exams!

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.280
I'm aiming to be a life guard!

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:41.580
I didn't ask you!

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.580
There's going to be a performance
at the Atelier. Wanna go see it?

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:45.850
Sure! I'd love to!

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:47.540
I'm not asking you!

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:51.650
Looks like he's finally
given up on the swim club.

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:53.060
Kyo has?

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:56.550
He hasn't been coming to the pool.
After acting so obsessed about it, too...

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:59.220
Gotta be girl trouble.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:02.530
Maybe he came on too strong to
Misaki-sempai and got rejected.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:05.090
Yeah, that sounds right.
The guy's such an idiot!

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:15.610
Shizuno-sempai?

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:27.520
So, what is it? You wanted to talk to me?

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:30.160
Well, you see... It's...

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:33.130
Look, Shizuno-sempai...

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.260
Did something happen
between you and Kyo?

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.660
What sort of thing?

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:40.400
Kyo just hasn't been himself.

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:42.970
I've never seen him like this...

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:43.670
And?

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:46.030
I was wondering if Kyo...

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:50.530
If maybe he told you
that he liked you, and...

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:52.070
It happened.

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:58.550
But, the truth is... It wasn't him
who did the confessing. It was me.

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:01.050
I told him I loved him.

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:09.160
If I said that, what would you do?

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:15.840
You really scared me!
I didn't think you'd joke about that.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:20.770
So why don't you tell me how
<i>you</i> feel about Sogoru?

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:24.580
What is Sogoru to you?

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:28.950
Oh, stop teasing me!
Kyo's just a boy I grew up with!

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:33.710
It's true he's struggling with something.

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:37.360
There's nothing I can do to help him, but...

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.560
If you can, maybe you can cheer him up.

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:41.690
See you.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:47.730
<i>It's true. I'm always the one who</i>
<i>ends up confessing to him.</i>

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:04.680
What is Sogoru to you?

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:11.420
That's a really good question.
What is Kyo to me?

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:17.520
A way to cheer Kyo up, huh?

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:19.160
Of course!

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:26.140
Now look, Kaminagi...

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:27.240
What?

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.080
I'll admit, there is water here,
like you said...

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.400
You love the water, don't you, Kyo?

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:34.910
Yeah. Except... EXCEPT!

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:37.490
I CAN'T SWIM HERE!

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.080
Um... Now, look...

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:41.960
Who said we were going
to the aquarium to swim?!

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:43.130
Now get dressed!

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.330
You really are a swimming addict, aren't you?

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:50.390
I chose a place with water for our date
because I wanted to cheer you up!

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:53.300
Oh, this is a date?
Then lemme ask you this:

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:56.800
Why'd you bring your digi-cam
and the script and a tripod?!

00:11:57.140 --> 00:11:59.970
Um... Well, it's kinda...

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:03.650
I thought we could do
some location hunting, too.

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:06.620
But that's secondary! Totally secondary!

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:09.650
Okay, let's get this show on the road!

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:11.020
Let the date begin!

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:13.520
Hey! Location hunting comes
second, right, Kaminagi?!

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:16.490
C'mon, answer me straight!
Am I just an afterthought on this?!

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:33.010
We get a new assignment and get
lucky almost immediately, Arque.

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:35.240
Who'd expect we'd run across a target this big?

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:36.070
Yeah.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:52.020
Enemy heavy transport "Viagem" sighted
by the Hraesvelg while on recon!

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:55.700
Course: 3-1-0, speed: 0-point-4-8!

00:12:55.970 --> 00:13:01.630
At this rate, Commander Isola's Dvaraka
will be in detection range in 90 minutes.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:05.130
Message from Hraesvelg.
They request Q.L. replenishment.

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:06.880
Replenishment, authorized!

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:08.940
Zegatank, stand by!

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:11.170
Commander, what about the Altair?

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:14.050
No. Save it for now.

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:17.490
Aye, sir! Scramble Lu-shen and May-yu!

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:19.010
What is it, Yehl?

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:24.230
That's right. This is a critical time in
seeing if Kyo is any use to us or not.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.650
I also want to see what sort of
assets Chris and Arque will make.

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:30.360
I don't expect you to
ever show any compassion.

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:33.770
Caladrius, prepare for launch!

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:41.440
Replenishment Q.L., charged and ready!

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:43.000
Moving to transmission chamber!

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:46.010
<i>Chamber seal release, confirmed!</i>

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:48.380
<i>Q.L. driver, conjunction!</i>

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:49.610
Entangle!

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.760
Confirm successful transmission of the Caladrius.

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:01.200
Then let's get started!

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:03.390
One last gift to Commander Isola!

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:04.600
Right.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:08.370
Front grip, weapons chamber coil! Output, okay!

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.300
Holonic field, forming!

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:12.170
Holonic rifles! Both hands!

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:30.590
Oh, man! Kaminagi, check this stuff out!

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:32.190
Red snapper! Shad!

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:33.160
A conger eel!

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:35.330
White tuna!

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:38.060
What is this, a big sushi bar for you?!

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:42.200
Well, no matter what,
he seems to be enjoying himself.

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:47.210
It's as tough as I expected.

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:49.970
But the Hraesvelg's firepower
is nothing to sneeze at!

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:03.360
Amazing!

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:06.660
Sending one unit up against the Viagem?

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:08.360
No wonder the commander wants them.

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:16.010
<i>A phony city. A phony life. A phony peace.</i>

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.970
<i>Everyone living without a clue.</i>

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:21.240
<i>About the Gards-orm invasion.</i>
<i>The destruction of mankind...</i>

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:24.600
<i>How they're just meta-bodies</i>
<i>preserved on a quantum server.</i>

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:32.350
<i>It's ironic. We, who've lost our physical</i>
<i>bodies, come to look at living things.</i>

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:34.680
Kyo?

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:38.860
I was just... Oh, yeah!

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:41.850
I was just thinking how much
this one looks just like you!

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.100
Oh, really?!

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:45.700
Agh! That hurt!

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:48.300
You jerk! You didn't have to hit me so hard!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.550
Aanvals launching from Viagem! Number: eight!

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:13.430
Take us in front of it!

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:13.920
Gotcha!

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:29.680
They're going toe-to-toe with us!

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:32.040
Switching holonic rifles to blade mode!

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:49.860
Restructuring right-side holonic wing!

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:57.860
Wha?! Arque!

00:16:58.140 --> 00:16:59.380
I'm fine!

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:02.000
I'm all right. Keep fighting!

00:17:03.610 --> 00:17:07.320
Let's finish this so we can finish that
bottle of Krug you like so much.

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:08.280
The Grand Cuvée?

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:09.880
It's vintage stuff!

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:17.730
Hraesvelg, withdraw from the battle zone at once!

00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:19.800
We can't transfer the Q.L. charge unless you do!

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:24.970
Multiple Ulvorfuls, closing!
Range 4,000, to the rear of the Hraesvelg!

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:27.770
We're giving Chris and Arque some
cover! Equip anti-air weaponry!

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:31.870
Roger! Reading arm-section conversion
data into the quantum conversion chamber!

00:17:31.870 --> 00:17:33.910
Transferring Q.L. load! Physicalizing!

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:34.880
Phalanx shot!

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:37.280
Physicalization, complete!

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:42.250
Oh!

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:44.350
Check out the streamlining on them!

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:47.480
God, if only I'd been born shaped like that!

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:55.890
<i>A phony existence. A phony life. A phony heart.</i>

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.730
<i>Can anyone say that we're really alive in any way?</i>

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:01.630
<i>We, who live merely as data?</i>

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:05.770
<i>Am I really "Kyo Sogoru?"</i>

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:09.140
<i>Am I really "here?"</i>

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:13.820
Man, that was a lot of fun!

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:17.650
Thanks a lot, Kaminagi!
You really cheered me up!

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:21.410
Liar.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.850
You've had something
on your mind all day.

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:27.500
You weren't having any fun at all!

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.520
You were just pretending
to enjoy yourself...

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:32.860
That's not true!
I swear, I had a blast...

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:38.330
You might be able to fool my eye,
but not the viewfinder on my camera!

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:44.180
Kyo, what's bothering you?

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:46.280
You can tell me, if you want.

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:49.150
I'm not going to act like I can
solve your problem, but...

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:53.020
But, it's hard for me.

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:57.290
It's so hard to just stand
and watch you being in pain.

00:18:57.460 --> 00:18:58.390
Kaminagi...

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:16.880
Viagem, changing course!
Heading now 0-3-5!

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:18.740
It's trying to withdraw from the battle zone!

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:21.780
Arque!

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.220
I'm fine.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:24.380
But!

00:19:25.090 --> 00:19:29.050
Why did we stay aboard the Oceanus, Chris?

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:31.130
Yeah, you're right.

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:34.520
Kyo?

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:45.110
Just one unit left!

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:45.900
Gotcha!

00:19:57.390 --> 00:19:59.180
K- Kyo, hold on a second...

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:02.780
You're warm, Kaminagi.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:07.430
You're alive, aren't you?
You're here with me, aren't you?

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:09.500
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:12.330
And I'm alive too, aren't I?
I'm here too, aren't I?

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:13.600
Here with you...

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:16.300
Kyo, you're squeezing too hard!
Let me go!

00:20:16.510 --> 00:20:19.130
No! I don't want to let you go.

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:20.470
Kaminagi...

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:27.380
It got away!

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:28.380
Forgive me.

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:31.350
No prob. It wasn't your fault.

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:34.650
We ran out of Q.L.
Next time, we'll get 'em for sure!

00:20:36.390 --> 00:20:38.380
Arque! Just hang on! Arque!

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:44.290
Oceanus! Emergency teleport! Hurry!

00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:45.720
No!

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:50.300
I'm not lying! Kaminagi, I really do!

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:56.780
It's no use. See? You can't lie to me, Kyo.

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:04.420
Go home without me, Kyo.

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:06.790
I think I left something inside.

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:08.350
Bye. I'll see you tomorrow!

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:18.790
I'm just... impossible...

00:22:51.260 --> 00:22:54.300
Reality is a lot harsher
than you think it is.

00:22:54.530 --> 00:22:58.130
But you don't feel any pain
unless it affects you directly.

00:22:58.130 --> 00:23:01.200
Struggle all the more, Kyo Sogoru!

00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:03.370
In the boundary between
the unreal and the real,

00:23:03.370 --> 00:23:09.310
I shall show you from outside both the
world you live in and your insignificant form!

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:13.350
Sis, you're totally out of character!

00:23:13.350 --> 00:23:14.780
- Next time, on Zegapain!
- Next time, on Zegapain!

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:16.420
"On the Other Side of the Water."

00:23:16.420 --> 00:23:19.020
My thoughts, never to be erased.
